# P2: the device profile of the PRODUCTION-SHAPED four-card verify: c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace is production c2-packed-tp4 (the verify audits OFF,
# the pinned sampler recorded in the verify trace, the budget cap on) plus the gate marker, so it is what traffic runs, minus the traffic
# limits. ONE job: status, an all-four reset, the tp4-prof-2 image (the replay-count read-back hook QWEN_FAST_PROFILE_DUMP_EVERY is image
# code, so the build step makes the image from this same commit), then two gate arms on the SAME four real-text coding prompts (4 x 4,096
# tokens; user 0 asks 192 tokens out, users 1-3 ask 64, all ignore_eos; the shapes are fixed in scripts/ci/ops_profile_plan.py, not here):
#   ops-twin   unprofiled: the per-round trace_ms, the [PACKED-*] and [PHASE] splits and the texts (the perturbation reference and the text
#              reference)
#   ops-trace  profiled: tracy (v138's recipe), op-support 20000 (200000 segfaults the dispatch thread: any other count is refused), the
#              CPP post-process only (no raw device log, which is tens of GB), a read-back after every 2nd verify replay of ANY kind (packed
#              or sequential) so no window overflows the per-core buffer, no prefill flush. One container gives 4-live 64-row rounds, then
#              3- and 2-live padded rounds as users 1-3 finish, then user 0 alone on the 1/2/4-row sequential engines.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a
# throwaway commit of tp4/next-3-prof and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry. ONE IMAGE FOR
# THE JOB: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image the build step makes from this same commit.
# NEVER CANCEL this job once the gate step has started: the profiler writes as root, and a cancel can leave root-owned files that break the
# next checkout (the workflow's always() hand-back step keeps the CPP report and prunes, but a killed container can still be writing). A
# segfault in read_core_data_from_completion_queue is INFRA: do not raise op-support.
# Disk: the build needs room and the profile tree up to 4 GB; the guard stops the arm at 4 GB of profile output or 85% disk, and the gate
# will not start at 80%. NEVER delete the base image the build starts from (the P8 base, qwen-fast-serving:ci-be9e184e); grep the
# Dockerfiles for FROM before deleting any image.
# Duration (estimate): status 1-2 min; reset and heal 3-6 (up to 12); build 18 typical (at most 90); ops-twin 15-40; ops-trace 30-60 (a cold JIT of
# every profiler-define kernel, the same streams, about 25 read-backs, the close): 1.5 / 2.5 / 3.5 hours. The gate refuses to start if its
# worst case (ops-twin 65 min, ops-trace 105 min, plus overhead per arm) does not fit the step and job time left.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset build gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-prof-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-twin,ops-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
